  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 117 PM CST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\nOnce the frontal boundary clears the area by Sunday afternoon,\nmuch cooler and drier weather will filter into the region.\nSunday will yield a wide range of afternoon highs, as\ntemperatures behind the front will only climb into the low to\nmid 50s. Meanwhile, areas closer to south-central Missouri that\nreceive peak heating before the front's arrival could see\ntemperatures in the low to mid 60s.\n\nLooking ahead to Thanksgiving week, temperatures will drop \nbelow normal, with daily highs in the 40s to low 50s, and \novernight lows dipping into the 20s. We'll need to monitor any\nchances for additional precipitation midweek towards the end of\nthe week, as upper level systems could influence the return of\nrain chances. There's still much uncertainty however, with the \ncurrent forecast remaining dry (<10% pops).",
